# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug
target

# The reader's gzipped corpus start-up cache, written beside data/kjv.jsonl
# when the repo itself is the data home. Regenerated; never commit.
*.idxcache

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# .NET build output (from the C# binding demo)
**/bin/
**/obj/
# …but NOT Rust's src/bin/ crate-binary sources (e.g. the pure-bindgen tool),
# which the broad **/bin/ rule above would otherwise swallow.
!**/src/bin/
!**/src/bin/**

# RustRover
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/

# Personal study data written when the repo root is the data home (dev/testing);
# never commit — the reader's own tags/weaves/threads/notes.
/tags/
/weaves/
/threads/
/notes/
/memory/

# Android signing keystores — the app's permanent signing identity. NEVER
# commit; keep it in a password manager, and feed CI via the
# ANDROID_KEYSTORE_BASE64 GitHub secret (see .github/workflows/release.yml).
*.jks
*.keystore

# Web shell (apps/web) build artifacts — regenerated by npm run pack:data / pack:wasm / build
apps/web/node_modules/
apps/web/dist/
apps/web/public/pack/
apps/web/public/pure_ffi.wasm
